        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: drop idle sleeps from insanity 5, 7, 8, 9",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: drop idle sleeps from insanity 5, 7, 8, 9\n\nTests 7, 8 and 9 sleep 60 after failing the clients and again at\nthe end of the test, and test 5 sleeps $TIMEOUT after the OSTs\nare back. Nothing depends on them.\n\nA failed client is unmounted with umount -f and does not\ndisconnect, but the live client's rm of its test file blocks on\nthe failed client's lock until the servers evict it, by blocking\nAST timeout or the ping evictor (about 100s). So the eviction is\nalready done before the first sleep starts, and the MDS and OST\nfailures that follow find its old exports gone, as before. The later\nsteps wait for what they need themselves, and test 5 already\nwaits for its background clients_up jobs.\n\nThe sleep 5 delays that let a background clients_up start before\nthe next failure are kept.\n\nTest time on a 1 MDS, 1 OSS (3 OSTs), 2 client rocky9 cluster:\n        before   after\ntest 5    64s     44s\ntest 7   256s    133s\ntest 8   276s    155s\ntest 9   257s    137s\n\nThis saves about 380s per insanity run, about 6900 runs per 30\ndays, or about 730 hours of test time.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=insanity\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I523e6f0d38e4688c5297e8d0e778812c08310705\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70257\nReviewed-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
